# Per-path token CHAIN ceilings, gated by `sherd budget` (V9). The format is
# itok's and sherd's, reused rather than reinvented.
#
# A chain is the cost of REACHING a node: root, every ancestor, and the node
# itself, which is what a reader pays before seeing any code. Longest
# matching prefix wins, so every node carries its own row.
#
# Set 2026-09-26 at ~25% above measured (`sherd budget`: root 5,217 · src
# 5,501 · largest leaf src/lay 6,056), rounded up to 100. The slack is so a
# legitimate addition does not force a raise; a raise is a reviewed commit
# with its reason. Every chain pays the root, so a row added to the root
# SPEC.md is billed 19 times.
